LibreQuake (apps/quake)

Engine (engine/)
  Chocolate Quake 2.1.0, by Henrique Barateli and contributors, based on
  the Quake source code by id Software (1996-1997).
  License: GNU General Public License, version 3 (engine/LICENSE).
  Source: https://github.com/Henrique194/chocolate-quake, tag
  chocolate-quake-2.1.0 (commit 8ee22175e3a5613e94ad2f9776aadc428b948cf3),
  with frunk.store's changes for the browser in
  engine/chocolate-web.patch (also tools/quake/chocolate-web.patch in
  https://github.com/RobertPKyle/frunk-store, whose tools/build-quake.mjs
  builds it). The complete patched source the build came from, with its
  build script (web/build.sh), is engine/chocolate-quake-2.1.0-web-src.tar.gz.
  The changes: one frame per screen refresh, controllers and touch handed
  in by the page, saving from the page, music played by the page,
  single player only (no sockets in a browser), windowed modes only, a
  4 MB stack, and a fix for strings longer than 256 characters overrunning
  a buffer when a game was saved.

Game (librequake/)
  LibreQuake 0.09-beta, the "lite" release, by the LibreQuake project and
  its contributors (librequake/CREDITS).
  https://github.com/lavenderdotpet/LibreQuake
  Art, models, sounds and music: BSD 3-Clause license (librequake/COPYING).
  Game code (progs.dat in the paks): GNU General Public License, version 2
  (librequake/COPYING-GPL2); its QuakeC source at the release's tag
  (commit d1515ca9bc01e590f2d54dc496f55c9a4ed72369) is
  librequake/librequake-0.09-beta-qcsrc.tar.gz.
  See librequake/README-IMPORTANT-LICENCE-INFO.
  The paks are gzipped here for downloading and unpacked by the page; they
  and the music are otherwise unchanged from the release's lite.zip
  (SHA-256 428e736b2f01d953e09a08c60bee975bdc4a0ac2219e97fa095c8af41754da83).

